bution, the same as { "commit": "", "pr": "", "sessionUrl": false }. Setting it to true is the same as leaving it out. Older Claude Code versions reject true or false here, so use the object form in settings files shared across versions.')},attributionProject:()=>h().optional().describe(`The claude.ai Project this session names for your organization's usage reports: the Project's UUID, or its ID starting with "claude_proj_". An empty string names none and stops lower-precedence files from naming one; the organization default still applies. Sent only when Claude Code uses your claude.ai login, connects directly to the Anthropic API, is not in a cloud session, and CLAUDE_CODE_ATTRIBUTION_HEADER is not 0. CLAUDE_CODE_ATTRIBUTION_PROJECT takes precedence over it. Set in managed settings, it overrides people's own settings files. A project's .claude/settings.json and settings.local.json count only once the folder is trusted; for runs in a folder nobody has trusted, such as CI, use CLAUDE_CODE_ATTRIBUTION_PROJECT.`),attributionProjectPolicy:()=>R({default:h().optional().describe('The Project used when neither CLAUDE_CODE_ATTRIBUTION_PROJECT nor attributionProject names one: its UUID, or its ID starting with "claude_proj_".')}).optional().describe("Your organization's default for attributionProject. Only honored from managed settings (server-managed, MDM / OS policy, or managed-settings.json); ignored in user, project, local and --settings sources."),includeCoAuthoredBy:()=>x().optional().describe("Deprecated: Use attribution instead. Whether to include Claude's co-authored by attribution in commits and PRs (defaults to true)"),...!1,...!1,includeGitInstructions:()=>x().optional().describe("Include built-in commit and PR workflow instructions in Claude's system prompt (default: true)"),permissions:()=>rr(()=>LZ(e)).describe("Tool usage permissions configuration"),model:()=>h().optional().describe("Override the default model used by Claude Code"),fallbackModel:()=>P(h()).op